.TH UFT 1 "February 2026" "uft 3.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uft \- bulk file transfer over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uft
.RB [ \-H
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR user ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR path ]
.RB [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uft
transfers large directory trees (100K+ files) over SSH using the fastest
available method. It auto-detects tools on both ends and picks between
tar pipes, netcat streams, or parallel rsync.
.PP
Designed for bulk image/frame downloads where per-file overhead kills
performance. A single tar stream avoids the SSH handshake-per-file
penalty that makes scp/sftp slow on large file counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR
Remote hostname or IP address.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
SSH username.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remote\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Source directory on the remote host.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-local\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Local destination directory.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Transfer mode. One of:
.RS
.TP
.B auto
(default) Pick the fastest available mode.
.TP
.B tar\-stream
Single tar pipe compressed over SSH. Fast, encrypted.
.TP
.B tar\-nc
Tar over netcat. Fastest option but unencrypted. Use only on trusted networks.
.TP
.B parallel\-rsync
Multiple rsync processes in parallel. Slower but supports resume.
.TP
.B benchmark
Run throughput benchmarks and report results.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compress " " \fIALG\fR
Compression algorithm: auto, lz4, pigz, zstd, gzip, none. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Number of parallel workers for rsync mode. Default: 8.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-streams " " \fIN\fR
Number of parallel netcat streams for tar\-nc mode. Default: 4.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
SSH port. Default: 22.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to SSH private key.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bwlimit " " \fIKB/S\fR
Bandwidth limit in KB/s. Applies to rsync mode natively; tar modes
require
.B pv
installed locally.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-jump " " \fIHOST\fR
SSH jump/bastion host, passed as
.BR ssh\ \-J .
The remote SSH connection is tunnelled through this host.
Note: tar\-nc mode is incompatible with jump hosts and automatically
falls back to tar\-stream.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude files matching
.IR PATTERN .
Can be specified multiple times. Patterns use tar/rsync glob syntax.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-from " " \fIFILE\fR
Read exclude patterns from
.IR FILE ,
one per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-copy\-links
Dereference (follow) symbolic links instead of preserving them.
Tar modes use \fBtar \-h\fR; rsync mode uses \fBrsync \-\-copy\-links\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-newer " " \fIDATE\fR
Only transfer files newer than
.IR DATE .
Accepts any date string understood by GNU tar's \fB\-\-newer\fR flag (e.g.
"2025\-01\-01", "2 days ago").
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-scan
Skip the remote file count and size scan during preflight. Useful when
scanning is slow on very large directories (millions of files). Disk
space checks and time estimates are unavailable when this is set.
.TP
.BR \-\-keep\-logs " " \fIN\fR
Keep the
.I N
most recent session logs and prune older ones. Default: 20.
Set to 0 to disable rotation (keep all logs).
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the configuration file. Default:
.IR ~/.uftrc .
See
.B CONFIG FILE
below.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Resume a previously interrupted transfer. Works with parallel\-rsync mode.
Completed directories are tracked and skipped on re\-run.
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Verify file counts and sizes after transfer (default: on).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Skip post-transfer verification.
.TP
.B \-\-checksum
Spot-check MD5 hashes on 100 randomly sampled files after transfer.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Run preflight checks only. Shows file counts, sizes, disk space, and
a time estimate without transferring anything.
.TP
.B \-\-tuning
Print network and kernel tuning tips.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.BR \-\-local\-ip " " \fIIP\fR
Override the auto-detected local IP address. Used by tar\-nc mode
when the remote host sends data back over netcat.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.SH TRANSFER MODES
.SS tar\-stream
Pipes \fBtar\fR through a compressor into a single SSH connection.
No per-file overhead \(em transfer time depends on total data size
and bandwidth, not file count. Picks the fastest cipher available
(typically aes128-gcm with AES-NI). Best for first-time bulk
downloads, especially with high file counts over high-latency links.
.SS tar\-nc
Same as tar\-stream but replaces SSH with raw TCP via netcat.
No encryption overhead. Can split across multiple parallel streams.
Only safe on private networks.
.PP
Not compatible with jump hosts; automatically falls back to tar\-stream
when \fB\-\-jump\fR is set.
.SS parallel\-rsync
Runs N rsync processes over a shared SSH multiplexed connection.
Each process handles a top-level subdirectory. Tracks progress in
a manifest file so interrupted transfers can resume. Uses size-based
bin-packing to balance work across workers. On high-latency links,
per-file overhead makes this slower than tar modes; on low-latency
links the difference is small. The only option when you need
incremental or resumable sync.
.PP
Actual speed depends on your network. Run \fBuft \-m benchmark\fR to
measure your link.
.SH CONFIG FILE
.B uft
reads a config file at startup. The default location is
.IR ~/.uftrc ,
overridden with
.B \-\-config
or the
.B UFT_CONFIG
environment variable. CLI flags always take precedence over config values.
.PP
Format is
.IR key\ =\ value ,
one per line. Comments start with
.BR # .
.PP
.nf
.RS
# ~/.uftrc
host = server.com
user = deploy
port = 22
key = ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
mode = auto
compress = lz4
jobs = 12
streams = 4
jump = bastion.example.com
keep_logs = 30
exclude = *.log
exclude = .git
exclude = __pycache__
newer = 2025-01-01
.RE
.fi
.PP
Supported keys:
.BR host ,
.BR user ,
.BR remote_path ,
.BR local_path ,
.BR port ,
.BR key ,
.BR mode ,
.BR compress ,
.BR jobs ,
.BR streams ,
.BR nc_port ,
.BR verify ,
.BR bwlimit ,
.BR local_ip ,
.BR symlinks ,
.BR jump ,
.BR keep_logs ,
.BR exclude " (repeatable),"
.BR exclude_from ,
.BR newer ,
.BR skip_scan .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UFT_HOST
Default remote host.
.TP
.B UFT_USER
Default SSH user.
.TP
.B UFT_REMOTE
Default remote path.
.TP
.B UFT_LOCAL
Default local path.
.TP
.B UFT_PORT
Default SSH port.
.TP
.B UFT_KEY
Default SSH key path.
.TP
.B UFT_MODE
Default transfer mode.
.TP
.B UFT_COMPRESS
Default compression algorithm.
.TP
.B UFT_JOBS
Default parallel job count.
.TP
.B UFT_STREAMS
Default netcat stream count.
.TP
.B UFT_JUMP
Default jump/bastion host.
.TP
.B UFT_NEWER
Default \-\-newer date filter.
.TP
.B UFT_EXCLUDE_FROM
Default exclude-from file.
.TP
.B UFT_SKIP_SCAN
Skip remote scan (set to "true").
.TP
.B UFT_KEEP_LOGS
Number of session logs to keep.
.TP
.B UFT_COPY_LINKS
Set to "true" to dereference symlinks.
.TP
.B UFT_CONFIG
Config file path (default: ~/.uftrc).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.uftrc
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.uft/logs/
Session logs.
.TP
.I ~/.uft/manifests/
Directory listings from remote scans.
.TP
.I ~/.uft/resume/
Resume state for parallel\-rsync mode.
.TP
.I ~/.uft/locks/
Transfer locks (one per destination path).
.SH EXAMPLES
Auto-detect fastest method:
.PP
.RS
uft -H server.com -u deploy -r /data/frames -l ./frames
.RE
.PP
Maximum speed on a trusted network:
.PP
.RS
uft -H 10.0.0.5 -u root -r /data/frames -l ./frames -m tar-nc -s 8
.RE
.PP
Resumable transfer with 16 workers:
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u admin -r /data -l ./data -m parallel-rsync -j 16
.RE
.PP
Resume after interruption:
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u admin -r /data -l ./data -m parallel-rsync --resume
.RE
.PP
Exclude patterns:
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u deploy -r /data -l ./data --exclude '*.log' --exclude '.git'
.RE
.PP
Exclude from file:
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u deploy -r /data -l ./data --exclude-from .uftignore
.RE
.PP
Only files newer than a date:
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u deploy -r /data -l ./data --newer '2025-06-01'
.RE
.PP
Transfer through a jump host:
.PP
.RS
uft -H internal.lan -u deploy -r /data -l ./data -J bastion.example.com
.RE
.PP
Skip scan on huge directories:
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u admin -r /giant-dataset -l ./data --skip-scan
.RE
.PP
Use a custom config:
.PP
.RS
uft --config ~/projects/.uftrc -r /data -l ./data
.RE
.PP
Dry run (preflight only):
.PP
.RS
uft -H srv -u admin -r /data -l ./data --dry-run
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Transfer completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Error (connection failure, missing arguments, disk space, etc).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by user (Ctrl-C).
